## Key Points

| Component | Role |
|---|---|
| `GadgetChainBuilder` | Constructs the serialized object graph that triggers `Runtime.exec()` during `readObject()` |
| `ChainedTransformer` | Chains multiple `Transformer` calls so output of one feeds input of next |
| `InvokerTransformer` | Calls arbitrary methods via reflection — the core of the gadget |
| `TiedMapEntry` + `LazyMap` | Ensures the chain fires during `HashSet.readObject()` → `hashCode()` |
| `DeserializationExploit` | HTTP client that delivers the payload to the vulnerable endpoint |

**Assumptions**: Target classpath includes `commons-collections:3.1` (or 3.2.1), endpoint performs `ObjectInputStream.readObject()` on request body, and target runs on a Unix-like OS. Replace `TARGET`, `ATTACKER_IP`, and command strings with your lab values.

